  {
   "title": "The pager went off at 3am",
   "slug": "the-pager-went-off-at-3am",
   "category": [
    "on-call",
    "incidents"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "Episode 88"
   ],
   "image": "racks.jpg",
   "excerpt": "Sanne Vermeulen has been on call for eleven years. She explains the incident review template she wrote after a payment queue ate 40,000 transfers.",
   "date": "2026-09-24",
   "content": "<!-- wp:audio -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg\"></audio><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Stand-in audio: “Grace Hopper”, told by Megan Smith for the White House (public domain). Replace with your episode file.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:audio -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-chapters\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-chapters\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=0\">0:00</a> Intro, and what broke this week</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=262\">4:22</a> Sanne’s first pager, 2014</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=905\">15:05</a> The 40,000 transfers</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=1690\">28:10</a> Writing the review template</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=2610\">43:30</a> Rotas that don’t burn people out</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=3240\">54:00</a> Picks</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show notes</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Added</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-added\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-added\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Sanne Vermeulen on writing an incident review nobody dreads.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://sre.google/sre-book/postmortem-culture/\">The postmortem chapter of the Google SRE book</a>.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Changed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-changed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-changed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Follow-up to episode 85: Jonas moved the last two services off the cloud. The bill went from €1,140 to €310 a month.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Fixed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-fixed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-fixed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>In episode 87 we said the PDF library had 14 maintainers. It has four. The other ten are bots.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Removed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-removed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-removed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Twelve minutes of Lieke’s microphone falling off the desk.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-panel\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-panel\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\",\"style\":{\"typography\":{\"fontWeight\":\"600\"}},\"textColor\":\"muted\",\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Guest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Sanne Vermeulen</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Leads on-call for a payments company in Antwerp. Keeps a paper notebook for every incident since 2014.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Transcript</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Read the transcript</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Lieke</strong> Sanne, what did you have for dinner the night of the 40,000 transfers?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Sanne</strong> Nothing. That’s the point. That’s why it’s the first question.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-x-small-font-size\">Machine transcript, corrected by Lieke.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Who maintains the PDF library?",
   "slug": "who-maintains-the-pdf-library",
   "category": [
    "open-source",
    "maintenance"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "Episode 87"
   ],
   "image": "cables.jpg",
   "excerpt": "Tomás Ferreira maintains a library on most phones in Europe. He is paid for about six hours a month of it. We talk money, burnout and saying no.",
   "date": "2026-09-17",
   "content": "<!-- wp:audio -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg\"></audio><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Stand-in audio: “The ENIAC Programmers”, told by Megan Smith for the White House (public domain). Replace with your episode file.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:audio -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-chapters\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-chapters\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=0\">0:00</a> Intro</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=340\">5:40</a> How Tomás became a maintainer by accident</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=1320\">22:00</a> The six paid hours</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=2280\">38:00</a> Saying no to a bank</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=2900\">48:20</a> Picks</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show notes</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Added</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-added\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-added\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Tomás on the week a security report arrived during his wedding.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://opencollective.com/\">Open Collective</a>, which pays his six hours.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Fixed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-fixed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-fixed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Episode 86: the WCAG version is 2.2, not 2.1. Hana wrote in.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-panel\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-panel\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\",\"style\":{\"typography\":{\"fontWeight\":\"600\"}},\"textColor\":\"muted\",\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Guest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tomás Ferreira</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Maintains an image-decoding library. Lives in Porto. Answers issues on Tuesdays only.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Accessibility audits that get fixed",
   "slug": "accessibility-audits-that-get-fixed",
   "category": [
    "accessibility"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "Episode 86"
   ],
   "image": "keyboard.jpg",
   "excerpt": "Hana Novák has filed around 3,000 accessibility bugs. Most were never fixed. She explains how she writes the ones that are.",
   "date": "2026-09-10",
   "content": "<!-- wp:audio -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Ada_Lovelace_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.mp3\"></audio><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Stand-in audio: “Ada Lovelace”, told by Megan Smith for the White House (public domain). Replace with your episode file.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:audio -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-chapters\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-chapters\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Ada_Lovelace_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.mp3#t=0\">0:00</a> Intro</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Ada_Lovelace_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.mp3#t=410\">6:50</a> Hana’s first audit</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Ada_Lovelace_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.mp3#t=1500\">25:00</a> The bug report template</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Ada_Lovelace_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.mp3#t=2400\">40:00</a> Keyboard-only Thursdays</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show notes</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Added</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-added\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-added\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Hana’s bug report template, with her permission.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Kwame’s rule: every pull request gets tested with the keyboard only.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Changed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-changed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-changed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We now publish transcripts before the episode, not after.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-panel\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-panel\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\",\"style\":{\"typography\":{\"fontWeight\":\"600\"}},\"textColor\":\"muted\",\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Guest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Hana Novák</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Accessibility auditor in Brno. Screen reader user since 2009.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Leaving the cloud, a bit",
   "slug": "leaving-the-cloud-a-bit",
   "category": [
    "infrastructure"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "Episode 85"
   ],
   "image": "hero.jpg",
   "excerpt": "Jonas Peeters moved a newspaper’s websites back onto its own servers. He is not evangelical about it. Here are the numbers.",
   "date": "2026-09-03",
   "content": "<!-- wp:audio -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg\"></audio><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Stand-in audio: “Grace Hopper”, told by Megan Smith for the White House (public domain). Replace with your episode file.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:audio -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-chapters\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-chapters\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=0\">0:00</a> Intro</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=280\">4:40</a> The €1,140 bill</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=1100\">18:20</a> What stayed in the cloud and why</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Grace_Hopper_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.oggvorbis.ogg#t=2200\">36:40</a> The night the switch died</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show notes</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Added</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-added\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-added\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Jonas’s cost spreadsheet, month by month.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Removed</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-removed\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-removed\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The part where Kwame explains Kubernetes. He was wrong and he knows it.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-panel\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-panel\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\",\"style\":{\"typography\":{\"fontWeight\":\"600\"}},\"textColor\":\"muted\",\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Guest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Jonas Peeters</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Runs infrastructure for a Ghent newspaper. Has a rack in a basement near Sint-Pieters.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Printers",
   "slug": "printers",
   "category": [
    "hardware",
    "drivers"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "Episode 84"
   ],
   "image": "terminal.jpg",
   "excerpt": "Nadia Haddad writes printer drivers. Everyone hates printers. Nadia explains why they are hard, and why that is mostly the paper’s fault.",
   "date": "2026-08-27",
   "content": "<!-- wp:audio -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg\"></audio><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Stand-in audio: “The ENIAC Programmers”, told by Megan Smith for the White House (public domain). Replace with your episode file.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:audio -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chapters</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-chapters\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-chapters\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=0\">0:00</a> Intro</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=300\">5:00</a> What a driver actually does</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=1400\">23:20</a> Paper is a physical object</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/The_ENIAC_Programmers_%28As_Told_By_U.S._Chief_Technology_Officer_Megan_Smith%29.ogg#t=2500\">41:40</a> Picks</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Show notes</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Added</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-diff-added\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-diff-added\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Nadia’s list of printers she would buy with her own money. It has two entries.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-panel\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-panel\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\",\"style\":{\"typography\":{\"fontWeight\":\"600\"}},\"textColor\":\"muted\",\"fontSize\":\"x-small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-muted-color has-text-color has-x-small-font-size\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Guest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Nadia Haddad</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Driver engineer in Liège. Has fixed a jam with a butter knife in front of a CEO.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
  },
